  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Consider the following reaction approaching equilibrium at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> atm pressure</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><munder><mover><mo>&#8652;</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mover><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></munder><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math></p><p>The standard Gibb&#39;s energy change <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mo>-</mo></mfenced></math>&nbsp;_____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>kJmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;(Nearest integer).</p><p>(Given : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn></math>)</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We know,</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi>eq</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi>eq</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math><br />Using gibbs free energy equation,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#916;G</mi><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>RTlnK</mi><mi>eq</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#916;G</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>RTln</mi><mn>10</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mole</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;(nearest integer)</p><p>Answer&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
}